WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:25.260
Hi, welcome back to the Wheel of Life online retreat.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:37.590
Now we've reached session eleven, and this session is called "How it all Begins."

00:00:42.489 --> 00:00:45.719
The outline that we talked about at the beginning of this retreat,

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:53.399
we reviewed some of the past retreats we've been doing lately,

00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:02.040
and we covered "how do negative emotions come up in our mind?"

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:12.059
Then we covered "how did those cause us to collect karma?"

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:23.489
Then we saw how those karmas take us through a whole life, even to death, and to the bardo (BAR DO), and to the next birth.

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:37.139
And then Pabongka Rinpoche, the teacher of this whole book,

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:45.389
he said, "Let's go look at another way this is presented, for example, by the First Panchen Lama,

00:01:54.640 --> 00:02:00.779
and Je Tsongkapa." And they like to use the the Wheel of Life teaching.

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:08.429
So we're going to start out with the Wheel of Life teaching. We're going to go through the Wheel of Life teaching now.

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:20.099
I chose as the image, it's a blind woman--it's an elderly woman, who cannot see well.

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:29.159
And for me, personally, this represents my stepmom.

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:35.309
Ever since I lost my real mother,

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.859
my stepmom Edie,

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:45.270
she married my father,

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:49.950
and she's had a long, beautiful life--she's a very fine person.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:57.329
And now she's losing her eyesight.

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:02.670
And they did many operations

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:08.400
and they say now they cannot fix it.

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:13.980
And she's slowly becoming blind.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:18.030
I spoke to her two days ago

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:23.189
and she keeps falling down, she keeps tripping on things.

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:30.929
She has trouble seeing steps, for example.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:37.679
Then I have another close friend--I'm going to show you his picture now, his name is Theo.

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:47.500
He's kind of our son--Veronica and me, that's our son.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:58.800
And he's an old dog and somebody kind of dumped him on us

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:05.460
and we were afraid that those people would kill him,

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:09.930
so we agreed to take him.

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:14.339
And the problem is, I don't know if you can see, but he's blind.

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:21.750
He's also deaf.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:24.720
So his life is very difficult.

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:28.839
You see another picture of him here

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:37.629
outside our house and he's headed towards a big piece of wood,

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:42.909
and we have to catch him because he will hit his head.

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:50.019
So these blind people, blind animals,

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:54.550
they have trouble

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:57.370
because they cannot see,

00:04:58.759 --> 00:05:00.759
they get into danger--

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:03.940
dangerous situations happen to them.

00:05:05.449 --> 00:05:08.978
And that's the story of the first link of the Wheel of Life.

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:15.159
Here we see the first picture of the Wheel,

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:21.940
and it's a painting of a blind man with a stick.

00:05:24.469 --> 00:05:30.639
And this, in the Wheel of Life, represents the first of the twelve links,

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:42.440
which is called "misunderstanding." People have called it "ignorance,"

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:50.020
which is sort of a translation of the Sanskrit, which is &lrm;avidyā,

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:57.460
which literally means "not seeing." "A" means "not."

00:05:59.599 --> 00:06:02.679
"vidyā" is related to "video"--it means "to see."

00:06:07.849 --> 00:06:11.289
And it means... people have translated it as "ignorance."

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:18.279
So I want you there, wherever you're sitting right now

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:27.510
watching this video, I'd like you to think for a minute about the difference.

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:35.459
What's the difference between the word "ignorance" and the word "misunderstanding."

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:44.459
And in the Abhidharma, which Stanley, again, is translating--

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:50.849
he's scheduled to finish in 26 years--

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:58.140
it says

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:04.770
ignorance, if you think about it, is for example like you don't know a certain person.

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:17.880
So I was thinking about a friend in my college time named Tom.

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:29.429
So I asked Stanley, "Do you know Tom?" He says, "No, Geshe-la. I wasn't even born at that time!"

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:36.359
So that's "not knowing Tom."

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:42.779
A-vidyā or ignorance.

00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:47.880
"I just don't know him."

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:57.629
So that's one kind of not knowing. 
But if I say to Stanley, "Do you know Tom,"

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:05.130
and I'm thinking about that Tom that I knew when I was in college,

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:16.920
and then Stanley misunderstands my question and he thinks I'm talking about some Tom that we both know nowadays,

00:08:25.599 --> 00:08:32.639
then he says, "Yeah, I know Tom," but he doesn't understand I'm talking about the Tom from a hundred years ago.

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:39.120
So now it's different.

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:41.700
In the first case,

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:45.510
I said, "Do you know that Tom that was in my college?"

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:51.540
and he says, "No, I wasn't born yet, Geshe-la."

00:08:55.029 --> 00:08:57.179
Or if I just say, "Do you know Tom," and

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:02.159
then Stanley makes a mistake and

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:05.609
he thinks I'm talking about another Tom,

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:10.580
that's a mis-understanding,

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:14.820
and that's different from not knowing Tom.

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:21.240
In the first case--ignorance or not knowing--

00:09:24.610 --> 00:09:26.729
it's just that you don't know this person.

00:09:29.649 --> 00:09:32.969
But with mis-knowing, mis-understanding,

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:38.370
it's more dangerous.

00:09:38.980 --> 00:09:44.640
So for example, he might go to that new Tom and say, "Oh, Geshe-la says you went to college together."

00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:53.279
Then that Tom will get upset, "I wasn't even born at that time!"

00:09:56.890 --> 00:10:02.699
So it's easy to imagine this picture of a blind person, or a blind dog ...

00:10:07.510 --> 00:10:09.510
their life is a kind of darkness,

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:16.570
they cannot even see Tom, for example.

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:21.969
But that's not actually what we're talking about in the Wheel of Life.

00:10:26.510 --> 00:10:28.569
We're talking about you misunderstand.

00:10:29.180 --> 00:10:34.690
So really, it's not that you're blind; it's that you are seeing something that's not there.

00:10:46.490 --> 00:10:53.469
And then you get in trouble, because the whole topic we are covering in the lam rim (LAM RIM) right now is "how you get in trouble."

00:11:04.550 --> 00:11:06.550
So we're going to go back to the text now,

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:10.749
and we're going to read it together,

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:14.820
but please keep that in mind.

00:11:17.060 --> 00:11:22.040
I always translate avidyā or ma rikpa (MA RIG PA) as "misunderstanding,"

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:27.940
not as "ignorance."

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:30.300
It doesn't mean "you don't know";

00:11:32.990 --> 00:11:35.049
it means you "mis-know."

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:39.670
You think you know, but you don't know,

00:11:40.730 --> 00:11:42.730
and that's more dangerous.

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:46.270
Okay, here we go with the text.

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:52.000
dang po marikpa ni (DANG PO MA RIG PA NI) means 
"let's talk about the first of the twelve links."

00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:00.500
This is, as we said, misunderstanding.

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:04.913
Then Pabongka Rinpoche says korwar korway tsawa yin

00:12:04.913 --> 00:12:06.320
('KHOR BAR 'KHOR BA'I RTZA BA YIN)--

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:11.350
it means "this is the main

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:18.609
cause, or the root, of why we are circling around the circle of suffering life."

00:12:28.329 --> 00:12:34.829
Now the purpose of studying the ancient books,for example--if you come to the Mixed Nuts classes--

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:46.160
is to develop wisdom, we call it sherab (SHES RAB).

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:54.440
In Sanskrit, it's called prajñā.

00:12:56.340 --> 00:12:59.520
And in China, you know, it came to be pronounced

00:12:59.520 --> 00:13:00.580
bōrě bōluómì duō (摩訶般若波羅蜜多經)

00:13:05.860 --> 00:13:07.860
So this wisdom,

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:14.579
it has a special meaning in Buddhism. Wisdom in general, in English, is like

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:19.379
the intelligence of an old man from living a long life.

00:13:34.929 --> 00:13:37.079
But when we say "wisdom" in Buddhism,

00:13:39.999 --> 00:13:42.569
it has a different flavor and

00:13:43.929 --> 00:13:48.059
it means you see the real nature of the world around you.

00:13:54.369 --> 00:13:59.729
Here it says sherab kyi dak mepar sungwa
(SHES RAB KYIS BDAG MED PAR BZUNG BA)--"What does wisdom see?"

00:14:03.549 --> 00:14:08.309
dak mepa (BDAG MED PA) means it sees that "things are not themselves."

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:20.459
And I love the example that we learn when we go to the Diamond Cutter Institute programs.

00:14:29.320 --> 00:14:37.020
There's a life tool--they call it a life tool--called "The Two Husbands in the Kitchen."

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:49.290
And it's the story where a woman yells at her two kids on a Friday,

00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:57.119
and she hears herself yelling,

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:01.710
which plants a seed in her mind.

00:15:03.850 --> 00:15:05.850
Next week

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:07.860
she comes home,

00:15:08.200 --> 00:15:14.490
she walks in the kitchen, and her husband immediately yells at her and calls her stupid.

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:22.740
Then it's easy for that woman to think, "Oh, my husband yelled at me for no reason!

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:30.509
I didn't even say anything and he called me stupid!"

00:15:33.900 --> 00:15:38.060
So she's seeing a husband in front of her

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:44.760
who is yelling at her, "You are stupid!"

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:48.920
for no good reason.

00:15:50.560 --> 00:15:55.060
And she, and us, we will always say, "I didn't do anything and he yelled at me!"

00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:06.869
Now that mind which thinks the husband's yelling at me for no reason,

00:16:12.940 --> 00:16:18.150
that state of mind is link number one--it's misunderstanding.

00:16:22.810 --> 00:16:24.810
Why is it misunderstanding?

00:16:26.010 --> 00:16:32.510
It doesn't understand that that husband came from the seed in my own mind.

00:16:38.190 --> 00:16:44.360
It doesn't understand I planted that seed in my own mind last week when I yelled at my kids.

00:16:52.830 --> 00:16:55.400
So there's actually a second husband in the kitchen,

00:16:58.440 --> 00:17:00.650
which did come from her--

00:17:02.490 --> 00:17:04.550
it came from the seed in her mind.

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:08.480
That one really exists.

00:17:10.050 --> 00:17:15.919
It's like the teacher we meditated on in a previous session.

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:24.619
I did these beautiful things in my past life

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:29.420
and because of that I see this beautiful teacher.

00:17:32.310 --> 00:17:38.959
That's dependent origination. I yelled at my kids

00:17:41.610 --> 00:17:43.760
and depending on that came my husband,

00:17:49.740 --> 00:17:54.680
who is yelling at me. And a person who understands that--

00:17:56.730 --> 00:17:58.730
who has wisdom--

00:17:59.490 --> 00:18:05.240
when they walk in the kitchen and the husband says, "You're stupid!"

00:18:07.650 --> 00:18:10.040
and immediately this emotion comes up,

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:15.830
"Why did he call me stupid? I didn't say anything!"

00:18:17.250 --> 00:18:20.359
She's able to stop that emotion

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:27.320
because she attended the online Wheel of Life retreat.

00:18:30.599 --> 00:18:36.289
She understands that husband who is not her fault is not real.

00:18:41.759 --> 00:18:44.389
If you want to say it in a mysterious way,

00:18:47.669 --> 00:18:54.498
she understands the husband she thought was there was not there. She understands her husband is not her husband.

00:19:00.869 --> 00:19:03.978
And that's what the lam rim means here

00:19:06.690 --> 00:19:08.690
when it says

00:19:09.149 --> 00:19:13.039
sherab kyi dak mepar sung--your wisdom perceives

00:19:15.450 --> 00:19:17.720
that the person is not the person.

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:22.340
Now you know what that means.

00:19:23.399 --> 00:19:28.518
The person who didn't come from you in the kitchen is not a person.

00:19:33.419 --> 00:19:36.589
Now there's an important word here: la (LA).

00:19:39.509 --> 00:19:41.509
It's not Los Angeles, okay.

00:19:44.249 --> 00:19:46.249
It means, "but."

00:19:48.570 --> 00:19:55.909
Wisdom understands the husband in the kitchen who yells at me for no reason doesn't exist,

00:20:01.679 --> 00:20:06.829
but misunderstanding, link number one in the Wheel of Life,

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:10.970
it says "Oh, oh,

00:20:11.999 --> 00:20:14.509
why is he yelling at me? I didn't do anything!"

00:20:18.299 --> 00:20:20.748
It's looking at the husband completely wrong.

00:20:23.340 --> 00:20:26.929
It is misunderstanding the husband.

00:20:29.609 --> 00:20:31.609
Then at the same moment,

00:20:32.549 --> 00:20:35.418
it's misunderstanding everything in the kitchen also.

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:39.540
The refrigerator.

00:20:39.940 --> 00:20:41.940
Who paid for the refrigerator?

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:46.350
How did I get the money for the refrigerator behind my husband right now?

00:20:53.200 --> 00:21:00.840
sherab--wisdom--it understands. "Oh, I helped another person buy something for their home, therefore I have a refrigerator."

00:21:07.840 --> 00:21:14.610
But misunderstanding looks at the refrigerator, "That's MY refrigerator."

00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:19.919
Why? "I worked for money, I bought that refrigerator!

00:21:22.120 --> 00:21:24.120
It comes from the store."

00:21:26.260 --> 00:21:30.690
Now, if you don't understand that your husband yelling is coming from you

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:40.950
and if you don't understand that you got the refrigerator in your kitchen because you helped someone else to get something,

00:21:46.600 --> 00:21:49.919
then you'll get angry about that husband and

00:21:51.820 --> 00:21:55.019
if someone tries to take your refrigerator you will fight with them.

00:21:58.390 --> 00:22:01.950
Then you are living in the Wheel of Life, and the Wheel of Life is always...

00:22:02.230 --> 00:22:05.219
the name of the Wheel of Life is suffering Wheel of Life.

00:22:13.780 --> 00:22:15.780
Okay, so now we can go to the text.

00:22:18.550 --> 00:22:21.960
ma rikpe--misunderstanding things like this,

00:22:24.700 --> 00:22:26.700
"Oh, that husband,

00:22:27.010 --> 00:22:29.010
he comes from his side,

00:22:29.920 --> 00:22:31.920
he decided to get angry."

00:22:33.850 --> 00:22:38.789
gam (GAM) means "or." chu la mik ne (CHOS LA DMIGS NAS)--this chu (CHOS) doesn't mean "dharma."

00:22:40.630 --> 00:22:42.749
It means "an object" in the kitchen.

00:22:45.460 --> 00:22:52.590
Like the refrigerator. "That came from the store. I bought it with my money."

00:22:56.440 --> 00:23:03.450
Misunderstanding doesn't understand that I have a refrigerator because I got money because I helped other people to get money.

00:23:10.860 --> 00:23:16.780
Then, rang gi tsennyi kyi drupar dzin (RANG GI MTSAN NYID KYIS GRUB PAR 'DZIN)--
it holds that the husband exists out there from his own side.

00:23:20.760 --> 00:23:25.100
And it holds that the refrigerator exists out there from its own side.

00:23:29.500 --> 00:23:32.000
And the pen is coming from the pen.

00:23:33.140 --> 00:23:41.020
Then rikpa yeshe dang dzin tang ngu gel (RIG PA YE SHES DANG 'DZIN STANGS DNGOS 'GAL)--
Those two states of mind are in direct contradiction.

00:23:47.080 --> 00:23:52.110
Wisdom says, "Oh, my husband's yelling at me because I yelled at my kids last week."

00:23:56.110 --> 00:24:03.689
Wisdom says, "I have a refrigerator in my kitchen because I helped someone else to get some money."

00:24:11.500 --> 00:24:13.500
Ignorance thinks,

00:24:13.990 --> 00:24:15.990
sorry, misunderstanding thinks,

00:24:17.320 --> 00:24:19.559
"He's yelling at me for no reason,

00:24:21.580 --> 00:24:24.210
and that refrigerator, I worked for that refrigerator."

00:24:26.559 --> 00:24:33.869
So there's two states of mind, and one of them is completely mistaken,

00:24:38.230 --> 00:24:42.569
therefore we call it mis-understanding.

00:24:45.010 --> 00:24:51.569
And it's kind of like de ni mongpa longwa tabu shik go
(DE NI RMONGS PA LONG BA LTA BU ZHIG GO)--
And that's similar

00:24:53.890 --> 00:25:01.210
to a person who doesn't know what's going on at all; they are completely blind, like my dog Theo.

00:25:09.890 --> 00:25:15.520
And if you are blind in this way, if you are blind about what's real ...

00:25:19.220 --> 00:25:25.060
My blind stepmom, she falls off the steps and recently she cut open her chin,

00:25:31.430 --> 00:25:35.919
and my blind dog, he walks around the house and he hits his head on the wall.

00:25:42.200 --> 00:25:44.200
Those people who don't have wisdom,

00:25:46.130 --> 00:25:48.520
who misunderstand the husband and the refrigerator,

00:25:50.630 --> 00:25:52.749
in that sense, they are blind.

00:25:58.790 --> 00:26:03.040
Then Pabongka Rinpoche says, "You know what, there are two kinds of this kind of misunderstanding."

00:26:06.890 --> 00:26:12.160
de la lendre mongpa dang (DE LA LAS 'BRAS LA RMONGS PA DANG)-- 
Some people don't understand karma.

00:26:15.470 --> 00:26:18.370
They don't understand that the husband came from what they did before.

00:26:23.270 --> 00:26:26.080
They don't even know about karma.

00:26:28.700 --> 00:26:31.299
Maybe they heard the word karma or Yè lì,

00:26:34.370 --> 00:26:37.479
but they have no idea about the laws of karma.

00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:44.080
So that's one kind of blindness--here it's called "darkness."

00:26:48.530 --> 00:26:51.550
Then there's a second kind of misunderstanding--

00:26:54.350 --> 00:26:57.910
about emptiness, the real nature of things.

00:27:00.799 --> 00:27:05.799
To put it very clearly, simply, and correctly,

00:27:10.820 --> 00:27:14.080
the husband I thought was in the kitchen,

00:27:17.360 --> 00:27:19.839
the husband who yelled at me for no reason,

00:27:23.150 --> 00:27:30.789
that husband was never in the kitchen, he's not in the kitchen now, he will never be in the kitchen, because he cannot exist.

00:27:40.159 --> 00:27:42.159
So two kinds of not-knowing.

00:27:44.660 --> 00:27:49.180
Number one: "Do you know about karma, the laws of karma, the rules of karma?"

00:27:52.260 --> 00:27:55.460
"No, I never studied it."

00:27:56.320 --> 00:27:58.320
And then the second kind,

00:27:59.330 --> 00:28:04.840
"Do you realize that the husband you thought was in the kitchen was never in the kitchen?"

00:28:10.490 --> 00:28:18.400
So obviously the second one is more dangerous. You can hit your head on the wall more strongly.

00:28:23.840 --> 00:28:29.380
Okay, we have a few minutes left, let's go on to the second link of the Wheel,

00:28:33.289 --> 00:28:40.389
which is called "fresh karma," and the picture is a potter making pots.

00:28:44.030 --> 00:28:47.379
There's a very simple example of fresh karma.

00:28:52.579 --> 00:28:57.309
Fresh karma is the seed you planted in your mind just now.

00:29:03.169 --> 00:29:10.028
In the kitchen your husband called you stupid and you say, "I'm not stupid, you're stupid!"

00:29:13.190 --> 00:29:20.709
Your misunderstanding about the husband just caused you to do... link number one caused link number two.

00:29:25.820 --> 00:29:31.140
And you made a fresh karma. Now Stanley, for a hundred dollars.

00:29:34.040 --> 00:29:35.420
Ready?

00:29:38.840 --> 00:29:44.180
Let me think about it. I forgot the question.

00:29:47.179 --> 00:29:52.418
Yeah, so she doesn't understand the husband. She misunderstands.

00:29:55.429 --> 00:29:58.358
Misunderstanding mind says, "I didn't do anything--he just yelled at me."

00:30:01.099 --> 00:30:06.279
And because of the misunderstanding mind, link number one, blind man,

00:30:12.919 --> 00:30:15.309
then she makes a fresh karma,

00:30:16.639 --> 00:30:18.968
then she says, "I'm not stupid--you're stupid!"

00:30:21.079 --> 00:30:23.109
She just put a new seed in her mind.

00:30:26.140 --> 00:30:31.200
What will happen from that seed? Hundred  dollar question...

00:30:35.140 --> 00:30:38.520
(What will happen from that seed?) Yeah, when it opens.

00:30:40.480 --> 00:30:43.360
The husband... the kids!

00:30:44.120 --> 00:30:47.480
Fifty dollars. He guessed half-way wrong. Fifty dollars.

00:30:52.960 --> 00:31:00.420
Of course, the husband will yell at her, but the big idea is the kids will be bad next week.

00:31:06.400 --> 00:31:08.400
Then she will yell at them.

00:31:09.190 --> 00:31:12.870
She will plant a new seed. That seed will open in the kitchen.

00:31:14.289 --> 00:31:17.969
And that's the Wheel of Life--sansara.

00:31:20.980 --> 00:31:25.890
Kids--husband, kids--husband, kids--husband. Yell, yell, yell, yell, yell, yell, okay?

00:31:25.890 --> 00:31:29.129
So we have many small sansaras--many small wheels.

00:31:33.789 --> 00:31:35.999
But right now in the kitchen,

00:31:37.690 --> 00:31:40.020
that seed is still fresh karma.

00:31:42.130 --> 00:31:44.489
And you know, I like to garden.

00:31:47.289 --> 00:31:50.999
I enjoy planting watermelons. I'm going to plant some watermelons this week, in fact.

00:31:54.490 --> 00:31:56.939
When you first put the seed under the dirt,

00:31:58.840 --> 00:32:00.840
that's link number two.

00:32:00.909 --> 00:32:02.909
That's making new pots.

00:32:04.690 --> 00:32:06.690
Let's go to the text.

00:32:07.480 --> 00:32:13.469
nyipa duje ni (GNYIS PA 'DU BYED NI)--the "second" link of the Wheel, 
which is called "making fresh karma,"

00:32:16.840 --> 00:32:21.360
le ka jepa tar (LAS KA BYED PA LTAR)--it's just like working, like building something.

00:32:26.620 --> 00:32:32.459
ma rikpe kun ne lang te (MA RIG PAS KUN NAS BSLANG STE)--
you are motivated by your misunderstanding of your husband,

00:32:39.370 --> 00:32:41.370
and then you do things.

00:32:42.010 --> 00:32:46.260
yang si pungpo ngunpar dujepay le jepa yinpe
(YANG SRID PHUNG PO MNGON PAR 'DU BYED PA'I LAS BYED PA YIN PAS)--
and you do

00:32:46.840 --> 00:32:51.630
karma, which is going to produce a new body and mind for you in the next life.

00:33:00.059 --> 00:33:04.099
You are like a potter who's making pots for the next life.

00:33:10.440 --> 00:33:14.179
And there are three traditional kinds of karma you can make,

00:33:17.309 --> 00:33:20.898
and this is a little different from the usual presentation.

00:33:26.279 --> 00:33:31.819
Usually we just say your good karma is what produces happy things in your life,

00:33:37.880 --> 00:33:40.480
and bad karma is what makes bad things in your life,

00:33:42.740 --> 00:33:49.820
and neutral karma made these little lines on this coffee cup that nobody cares about.

00:33:56.879 --> 00:34:00.949
But here we have a slightly different traditional presentation.

00:34:05.580 --> 00:34:10.790
lendre la mongpay ma rikpe kun ne lang te
(LAS 'BRAS LA RMONGS PA'I MA RIG PAS KUN NAS BSLANG STE)--
if you have this kind of

00:34:11.639 --> 00:34:15.979
misunderstanding where you never learned about karma and the result of karma,

00:34:22.409 --> 00:34:26.838
if you never

00:34:26.839 --> 00:34:30.769
had the good seeds to meet a teacher who taught you about karma,

00:34:35.879 --> 00:34:39.199
then you will make sunam mayinpa (BSOD NAMS MA YIN PA). 
It's called sunam mayinpa.

00:34:40.919 --> 00:34:42.919
You will do bad things:

00:34:43.980 --> 00:34:51.829
kill people, lie, steal things, okay? But if you have the second kind of misunderstanding,

00:34:54.030 --> 00:34:59.239
ne luk la mongpay ma rikpe
(GNAS LUGS LA RMONGS PA'I MA RIG PAS), 
which doesn't understand the real nature of your husband--

00:35:02.990 --> 00:35:08.469
the dependent origination of your husband that he came from yelling at your kids--

00:35:13.819 --> 00:35:21.609
that's a different kind of misunderstanding, and it's possible those people can do good deeds also.

00:35:24.980 --> 00:35:32.919
There's such a thing as good deeds which your mom taught you to do, but you don't understand karma.

00:35:39.109 --> 00:35:41.109
So you do good things.

00:35:41.599 --> 00:35:43.599
They're called "dirty good karma."

00:35:45.559 --> 00:35:48.069
You don't understand what you're doing and you do it.

00:35:51.950 --> 00:35:57.519
Those will take you to a good place which will finish, because you don't know why you are there.

00:36:06.000 --> 00:36:10.180
So, many of the good actions that people do are not good karma,

00:36:15.660 --> 00:36:18.600
if they don't really understand.

00:36:19.700 --> 00:36:24.220
So these three words in Tibetan: sunam,

00:36:27.230 --> 00:36:28.490
Non-sunam,

00:36:28.490 --> 00:36:29.930
and

00:36:29.930 --> 00:36:35.710
then we call "unshifting karma"--karma which will not detour to another place.

00:36:43.700 --> 00:36:47.230
The first one is dirty good karma.

00:36:49.940 --> 00:36:56.950
Yeah, you're going to go someplace pretty good, but you will suffer there also.

00:36:59.650 --> 00:37:02.190
Or you do bad karma

00:37:03.160 --> 00:37:07.950
and it doesn't matter where you go... you will go to what we call the desire realm,

00:37:11.770 --> 00:37:17.520
And you will suffer there. But there is a kind of a pretty strong good karma,

00:37:20.080 --> 00:37:27.870
here it is called mi yoway le (MI G-YO BA'I LAS)--
it will take you to the form realm or the formless realm, which we talked about already.

00:37:35.170 --> 00:37:39.540
And that karma is so good, so strong, that it won't detour,

00:37:43.000 --> 00:37:45.000
but still it's a suffering karma.

00:37:46.900 --> 00:37:49.050
Okay, so there we have the first two links.

00:37:51.760 --> 00:37:53.760
You don't understand your husband,

00:37:55.030 --> 00:37:57.030
so you yell back at him.

00:37:58.120 --> 00:38:00.120
What's that going to cause?

00:38:01.750 --> 00:38:03.750
Find out in session twelve.

00:38:05.590 --> 00:38:07.590
See you later and thank you Stanley.

